# 2️⃣ Many-to-Many N+1 Traps (EVEN WORSE)

### Entity example

```java
@ManyToMany
Set<Role> roles;
```

---

## 🔥 Why this is dangerous

Hibernate creates:

* Join table
* Extra joins
* Extra selects

Accessing:

```java
user.getRoles()
```

For N users:
→ **N+1 joins on join table**

This explodes **faster than OneToMany**.

---

## ❌ Worst mistake

```java
@ManyToMany(fetch = FetchType.EAGER)
```

This causes:

* Huge result sets
* Memory spikes
* Slow startup
* Broken pagination

---

## ✅ Correct Patterns

### ✔ Replace Many-to-Many with Join Entity

```java
UserRole
```

Now you control:

* Fetching
* Queries
* Indexing

---

### ✔ DTO projections

```java
select new UserRoleDTO(u.id, r.name)
```

Avoid entities entirely for APIs.

---

## 🧠 Senior Rule

> Many-to-Many is fine for domain modeling
> **Bad for read APIs**

