# 3️⃣ Kafka Consumers + JPA Pitfalls (THIS CAUSES DATA LOSS)

This one is critical.

---

## 🔥 Common WRONG pattern

```java
@KafkaListener
@Transactional
public void consume(Event e) {
    repo.save(entity);
}
```

Looks correct. It is **dangerous**.

---

## 🔴 What can go wrong

1. DB commit succeeds
2. Kafka offset commits later
3. App crashes in between
4. Message is re-consumed
5. Duplicate DB writes

💥 **At-least-once bites you**

---

## ✅ Correct Production Pattern

### ✔ Idempotency (MANDATORY)

```java
if (processedEventRepo.exists(eventId)) return;
```

---

### ✔ Manual offset commit after DB commit

```java
@KafkaListener
public void consume(Event e, Acknowledgment ack) {
    process(e);
    ack.acknowledge();
}
```

---

### ✔ Short transactions only

Never:

* Lazy load inside Kafka consumer
* Keep EntityManager open long

---

## 🧠 Senior Rule

> Kafka guarantees delivery, **not uniqueness**

Uniqueness is **your responsibility**.

